      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TRALEE SNICKAS (2) was very good last start when he led and kept going to win by 5.4 metres at Albion Park. Two-tome winner here an draws to push forward again so is a big chance to go back to back. GREAT ACHIEVER (3) had no clear run at the latest appearance so prepared to forgive that result. Good effort to win from a wide barrier at this circuit and distance prior. Likely to get the favours from this nice draw. Good enough to take out a race like this. KICK THE SWITCH (5) had a tough draw and raced parked so was far from disgraced when beaten 5 metres last week after filling a minor placing at the previous appearance here. Return to the front line. Big chance. TILLY JAYNE (6) has to come into calculations on the back of some strong recent form, winning here two back before a fifth at Albion Park last week. Yet to miss a place in six tries here, winning three.",
